## Component Name

**Path**: [src/components/OmronE5Types.h](../src/components/OmronE5Types.h)

**Revision History**:
- 2023-10-20: Initial documentation

A component interface for Omron E5 temperature controllers using Modbus-485 communication protocol. Defines register addresses, status bits, commands, and error codes for communication with Omron E5 devices.

## Requirements

### Dependencies
- RS485 communication module
- Modbus protocol implementation

### Configuration
```c
// Enable Omron E5 controllers in config.h
#define ENABLE_OMRON_E5
#define NUM_OMRON_DEVICES 1          // Number of connected Omron E5 devices
#define OMRON_E5_SLAVE_ID_BASE 1     // Base Modbus slave ID
```

## Features

- Comprehensive register mapping for Omron E5 controllers
- Status bit definitions for monitoring controller state
- Command definitions for controlling the device 
- Support for reading PV (Process Values), SP (Set Points), and other parameters
- Support for multiple Omron E5 devices on the same bus
- Error handling for communication issues

## Todos

- Add support for additional E5 series models
- Implement profile temperature control
- Add callback functions for status changes

## Example

```c
// Adding an Omron E5 controller to your components list
#ifdef ENABLE_OMRON_E5
  for (uint8_t i = 0; i < NUM_OMRON_DEVICES; i++)
  {
    uint8_t slaveId = OMRON_E5_SLAVE_ID_BASE + i;
    OmronE5* omronDevice = new OmronE5(
      this,                 // owner
      slaveId,              // Modbus slave ID
      100 + i               // component ID
    );

    if (omronDevice)
    {
      components.push_back(omronDevice);
      Log.infoln(F("Omron E5 controller initialized. ID:%d, Slave ID:%d"),
                 100 + i, slaveId);
    }
    else
    {
      Log.errorln(F("Omron E5 controller initialization failed."));
    }
  }
#endif
```

# 3-Position Analog Switch

*Revision: Initial documentation*

## COMPONENT OVERVIEW

The 3-Position Analog Switch (Pos3Analog) provides a way to read and control a physical three-position switch connected to analog input pins on an ESP32. It supports both local (physical) input and remote control via Modbus.

## REQUIREMENTS

### Hardware
- Two analog input pins connected to a 3-position switch
- ESP32 microcontroller

### Pin Configuration
- Up pin: Connected to the first analog input to detect "Up" position
- Down pin: Connected to the second analog input to detect "Down" position

### Dependencies
- [Component.h](../src/components/Component.h)
- [modbus/ModbusTCP.h](../src/modbus/ModbusTCP.h)
- [config.h](../src/config.h)
- [ArduinoLog.h](https://github.com/thijse/Arduino-Log)

## FEATURES

- Three distinct states (Up/Middle/Down)
- Modbus TCP integration for remote control and monitoring
- Switchable control modes (Local/Remote)
- State change notification system
- Configurable Modbus addressing

### Control Modes
- **LOCAL**: The physical switch determines the component state
- **REMOTE**: The value is controlled via Modbus 

### Modbus Registers
- Base Address + 0: Current 3-Position Switch Value (read-only)
- Base Address + 1: Control Mode (0=Local, 1=Remote) (read/write)
- Base Address + 2: Remote Value (read/write)

## USAGE

### Component Initialization

```cpp
#ifdef AUX_ANALOG_3POS_SWITCH_0
  Pos3Analog *switch3pos_0 = new Pos3Analog(
      this,                         // owner
      PIN_JOYSTICK_UP,              // upPin
      PIN_JOYSTICK_DOWN,            // downPin
      COMPONENT_KEY_ANALOG_3POS_SWITCH_0,  // id
      MB_ANALOG_3POS_SWITCH_0_ADDR  // modbusAddress
  );
  if (switch3pos_0)
  {
    components.push_back(switch3pos_0);
    Log.infoln(F("3PosAnalog_0 initialized. UpPin:%d, DownPin:%d, ID:%d, MB:%d"),
               PIN_JOYSTICK_UP, PIN_JOYSTICK_DOWN,
               COMPONENT_KEY_ANALOG_3POS_SWITCH_0, MB_ANALOG_3POS_SWITCH_0_ADDR);
  }
  else
  {
    Log.errorln(F("3PosAnalog_0 initialization failed."));
  }
#endif
```

## EXAMPLE

```cpp
// Configuration in config.h
#define PIN_JOYSTICK_UP 47     // UP direction pin
#define PIN_JOYSTICK_DOWN 48   // DOWN direction pin
#define COMPONENT_KEY_ANALOG_3POS_SWITCH_0 420
#define MB_ANALOG_3POS_SWITCH_0_ADDR 100  // Modbus start address

// In your application
// Create and initialize the 3-position switch
Pos3Analog *threePositionSwitch = new Pos3Analog(
    this, 
    PIN_JOYSTICK_UP,
    PIN_JOYSTICK_DOWN,
    COMPONENT_KEY_ANALOG_3POS_SWITCH_0,
    MB_ANALOG_3POS_SWITCH_0_ADDR
);

// Add to components list
components.push_back(threePositionSwitch);

// Later in your code
int switchPosition = threePositionSwitch->getValue();
if (switchPosition == Pos3Analog::E_POS3_DIRECTION::UP) {
    // Handle UP position
} else if (switchPosition == Pos3Analog::E_POS3_DIRECTION::MIDDLE) {
    // Handle MIDDLE position
} else if (switchPosition == Pos3Analog::E_POS3_DIRECTION::DOWN) {
    // Handle DOWN position
}
```

